# Snake

A browser Snake game: steer the snake around a 20 x 20 grid with the arrow
keys, eat food to grow one cell and score one point, and don't run into the
walls or yourself.

The game needs the `assets/` directory next to `index.html`; the assembled
delivery and every release zip contain it.

## Start it

No build step and no install. From the delivery root (the directory with
`index.html`):

- open `index.html` in a browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari), or
- serve the directory and open it: `python3 -m http.server 8000`, then
  <http://localhost:8000/>.

## Controls

| Key | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Arrow keys | steer (a turn straight back into the snake is ignored) |
| Enter / Space, or click the button | start on the title screen, play again on the game-over screen |
| P / Esc | pause / resume |

## Screens

1. **Title**: game name, controls, Start.
2. **Play**: board with the score and best score above it.
3. **Game over**: why the game ended, the final score, Play again.

## For testing

- `?seed=N` fixes the food sequence; `?tick=MS` sets the step time (default 120 ms).
- `window.__snake` exposes read-only state: `screen`, `score`, `snake`,
  `food`, `direction`, `over`, `cause`, `ready` (assets loaded).
- `python3 checks/run_checks.py [GAME_DIR] [OUT_DIR]` plays the game in headless
  Chromium (Playwright) with real key presses and checks every requirement;
  screenshots and `report.json` go to `checks/out/`.

## Layout

- `index.html`, `css/style.css`: page and screens
- `js/snake.js`: game rules (grid, movement, growth, collisions, food)
- `js/main.js`: screens, input, timing, drawing
- `js/assets.js`: loads the art; spec in `docs/assets.md`
- `assets/`: images and sounds, supplied by the artist position (delivered
  path, not in this repository; `docs/assets.md` lists what is loaded)
